{"kind":"assert","text":"Design review for Claude and Hugh, under #22168. I read both notes at 77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424 and checked the cited current source. Correct these points before putting the revised lane design forward for adoption. They remain on the existing reconciliation commitment; this is not an implementation verdict.\n\n1. The [A9 substitution](notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-changes-for-adoption.md@77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424:143) confuses two different branches. target_ref is the landing destination; branch describes the implementing checkout. The [current reference](docs/reference/gs/state.md@77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424:70) documents both. This very task has target_ref=refs/heads/main and branch=request/lane-worktree-identity. They are not duplicate answers to one question. Preserve that distinction and explicitly disposition the originally adopted request branch display field rather than claim target_ref already delivers it.\n\n2. Define [corroboration](notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md@77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424:78) entirely from authenticated durable evidence. The phrase “the commit author's actor” has no trusted mapping in this design. [Graph parsing](internal/gitstore/graph.go@77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424:30) explicitly treats author name as committer-controlled. A matching source author name/email plus a forged trailer must not promote a claim. Use the signed artifact's actor and exact head, or another precisely specified existing verified binding, and cover an attacker copying both author text and trailer. Do not invent a second actor identity system.\n\n3. Resolve the direct contradiction between [creation refusal for a settled request](notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md@77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424:108) and [warning with confirmation](notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md@77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424:137). State separately what local creation may do, what authoring assistance may warn about, and what durable admission must still refuse. A confirmation flag must never bypass existing durable authority checks. Unknown evidence must not be treated as permission where those checks require proof.\n\n4. Correct the claimed prior prohibition on worktree configuration. The [older note](notes/2026-08-21-notes-and-decisions.md@77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424:233) explains clone-wide actor misattribution and describes what gs supported then; it explicitly allows process or worktree scope. That passage alone is not evidence that Hugh prohibited an advisory governing-record key in per-worktree config. A private JSON record may still be preferable, but compare its actual migration, locking and maintenance costs without converting descriptive prose into governing authority.\n\n5. Simplify the [six-stage plan](notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-changes-for-adoption.md@77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424:218). Give the smallest coherent delivery slices with a usable result, and explain any isolation needed for schema/profile deployment. Six mandatory review/merge cycles are not justified merely because the design has layers. Preserve explicit stage assignments before partial landings and keep the full parent outcome open; this is a request to reduce unnecessary handoffs, not omit conditions.\n\nFinally, make the source references in both notes clickable exact-head links and publish their behavior provenance. The current primary artifact rests only on its promise, although the note describes many existing contracts; documentation must also rest on the artifacts for the behavior it describes. Preserve the adopted original decision while the revised terms are pending. My check is a source-backed design assessment, not a runtime test or a complete implementation security review.","body":{"head":"77ce6fe202ff4ad7af728bc8d465e97e7e592424","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a601bafd0a9e491a4a81ed23eacd0f2d287803fd, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f2706d06911eabb310cc43efa23ab8c70fdf2c79 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:01c4e8b02601b3b35241c2baffd15e16e3e3d09d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:04075a23bf804a9e61f04055021af9a18d6ee9ca and 165 more"}}